      "film_id": "fargo",
      "title": "Fargo",
      "year": 1996,
      "cinema": "ANU Film Group",
      "start": "2026-11-28T17:00:00",
      "description": "In a desperate attempt to get himself out of a financial jam, mild-mannered Minnesota car salesman Jerry Lundegaard (William H. Macy) hires a pair of criminal lowlifes (Peter Stormare, Steve Buscemi) to kidnap his wife and demand a ransom from her wealthy father. Or at least that’s the plan – but it’s not long before their inept bungling leaves three people dead. Soon, heavily pregnant local police chief Marge Gunderson (Frances McDormand) begins diligently investigating the murders, as Jerry hopelessly attempts to cover his tracks. Released in 1996, this quirky and hilarious crime comedy quickly became the Coen Brothers’ biggest hit to date. It went on to win two Oscars, including McDormand’s first Best Actress trophy, and has even recently spawned an acclaimed TV spin-off series set in the same continuity. So, is this macabre indie classic worth revisiting again on the big screen for i",
